7. Security
OUTPUT:
(a) As security for the performance of the Borrower's obligations under this Agreement, the Borrower hereby grants to the Lender a first priority security interest in all of the Borrower's present and after-acquired property, including, without limitation, all machinery and equipment acquired with the proceeds of the Loan.

(b) The Borrower shall execute and deliver to the Lender such additional documents and take such further actions as the Lender may reasonably request to perfect, maintain, protect, and enforce its security interest under this Agreement.

(c) The Guarantor hereby agrees to be bound by the security interest granted by the Borrower to the Lender under this Agreement and waives any rights it may have under the laws of the jurisdiction of its incorporation with respect to such security interest.

(d) The Borrower shall maintain, keep insured, and promptly pay all premiums in respect of all insurance policies required by the Lender to secure the Loan and its repayment.

(e) The Borrower shall keep the Lender informed of the location of all collateral securing the Loan and shall afford the Lender reasonable access to such collateral during normal business hours.

(f) In the event of a default by the Borrower under this Agreement, the Lender shall have the right to take possession of the collateral, sell the same, and apply the proceeds of such sale to the satisfaction of the Loan and its accrued interest.

(g) The Borrower shall not, without the prior written consent of the Lender, encumber, pledge, or otherwise dispose of any of the collateral securing the Loan. Any such encumbrance, pledge, or disposition shall be void and unenforceable against the Lender.

8. Interest and Fees
SOLUTION:
The Borrower shall pay interest on the outstanding principal balance of the Loan at a rate of twelve percent (12%) per annum, calculated on a 360-day year basis, and payable quarterly in arrears. The first interest payment shall be due on the date that is three (3) months after the Agreement Date.

The Lender shall be entitled to charge a fee of up to one percent (1%) of the original principal amount of the Loan for the costs and expenses incurred in connection with the origination of the Loan. This fee shall be payable at the time of disbursement of the Loan.

The Borrower shall also be responsible for all other fees and expenses incurred by the Lender in connection with the Loan, including, but not limited to, legal fees, appraisal fees, and other out-of-pocket expenses. These fees and expenses shall be payable as incurred.

9. Default and Remedies
SOLUTION:
(a) The Borrower shall be in default under this Agreement if it fails to make any payment when due, or if it breaches any of its other material obligations under this Agreement.

(b) Upon the occurrence of an event of default, the Lender shall have the right to declare all amounts outstanding under this Agreement immediately due and payable.

(c) In the event of a default by the Borrower, the Lender shall have the right to take possession of the collateral, sell the same, and apply the proceeds of such sale to the satisfaction of the Loan and its accrued interest.

(d) The Lender may also, in its sole discretion, pursue any other remedies available to it under applicable law, including, but not limited to, commencing a lawsuit against the Borrower or the Guarantor.

(e) The rights and remedies of the Lender under this Agreement are cumulative and not exclusive, and the Lender may pursue any one or more of such rights and remedies concurrently or sequentially, as it deems appropriate.

(f) The Borrower shall be liable for all reasonable costs, expenses, and attorneys' fees incurred by the Lender in connection with any enforcement of its rights under this Agreement, including, but not limited to, the costs and expenses of repossessing and selling the collateral.

(g) The Borrower shall not, without the prior written consent of the Lender, encumber, pledge, or otherwise dispose of any of the collateral securing the Loan during the period of default. Any such encumbrance, pledge, or disposition shall be void and unenforceable against the Lender.

(h) The Borrower shall promptly notify the Lender in writing upon the occurrence of any event of default. The Borrower's failure to give such notice shall not affect the Lender's rights or remedies under this Agreement.

